contentText:
It sounds like the apple doesn&#8217;t fall far from the musical tree in the Bieber household. In a new interview with Jake Shane on his Therapuss podcast, Hailey Bieber revealed that her 16-month-old son with Justin Bieber is already starting to take after the &#8220;Yukon&#8221; singer.

&#8220;Yeah he does. He&#8217;s been saying, &#8216;Baby, oh baby, oh baby oh.&#8217; And I&#8217;m like &#8216;whoa that is so crazy,'&#8221; Hailey said about son Jack Blues Bieber&#8217;s seeming obsession with his dad&#8217;s earworm breakthrough 2010 single &#8220;Baby.&#8221;

Bieber said Jack is already talking, a lot, ticking off some of his favorite words, which include one of Justin&#8217;s favorite leisure activities — &#8220;he says &#8216;basketball&#8217; all the time&#8221; — as well as &#8220;please,&#8221; which he knew how to say in sign langauge for a while before he could say it. Hailey said she loves being a mom, something she always knew she wanted, and when Shane wondered if the couple plan to have more kids, the answer was an unequivocal &#8220;yes.&#8221;

&#8220;I definitely want&#8230; I&#8217;m taking it one kid at a time,&#8221; said Hailey who spent a while bonding with Shane about their mutual obsession with the Claire Danes espionage series Homeland , which they binge together. &#8220;I definitely do want one more. I&#8217;m not in a rush, but I definitely want one more,&#8221; said Hailey. &#8220;Maybe I&#8217;ll have four more. Maybe I&#8217;ll have three. I don&#8217;t know, I really don&#8217;t know. I&#8217;m just taking it one day at a time.”

And while the public has not seen Jack&#8217;s face so far, Hailey showed Shane a picture of the toddler, noting that she recently got her son&#8217;s head shaved and he now looks &#8220;identical&#8221; to Justin. &#8220;Oh my God, I&#8217;m gonna be sick!&#8221; Shane howled when he saw the pic, dubbing the baby &#8220;adorable&#8221; and noting that he&#8217;s &#8220;the perfect mix of you guys.&#8221;

Hailey said she&#8217;s &#8220;more relaxed&#8221; about being a first-time mom than she expected, and you know she couldn&#8217;t help bragging about some of the cute things Jack does, like walking, running and kicking and throwing a soccer ball. &#8220;He&#8217;s into all of it,&#8221; she kvelled.

She also revealed which of her husband&#8217;s albums is her favorite, choosing JB&#8217;s 2013 R&B-tinged Journals compilation as her number one, followed by 2015&#8217;s Purpose , which featured such hits as &#8220;What Do You Mean?,&#8221; &#8220;Sorry&#8221; and &#8220;Love Yourself.&#8221; She also said she&#8217;s feeling the new albums from Kid LAROI, TEMS, Tame Impala and Olivia Dean, and, of course, she&#8217;s got Justin&#8217;s Swag album on repeat.

&#8220;It&#8217;s such a good listen to me top to bottom,&#8221; she said of JB&#8217;s 2025 album, which hit No. 2 on the Billboard 200 last summer. &#8220;Obviously maybe I&#8217;m a little biased, but like I think the sign of a great album is like when you&#8217;ve given it time and then you go back to listening to it and I just constantly keep going back to it.&#8221;

